We report a case of stiff-person syndrome associated with 
several autoimmune diseases. A 49-year-old male with type 
1 diabetes presented with a 6-month history of muscle rigid-
ity and spasms of his upper and lower extremities. Anti–glu -
tamic acid decarboxylase 65 antibody was elevated at 609 
nmol/L. Electromyography revealed continuous motor unit 
activity in agonist and antagonist muscles. He responded 
favorably to diazepam, baclofen, and intravenous immu -
noglobulin infusions. This case report describes stiff-person 
syndrome in association with pernicious anemia and diabe-
tes mellitus. A review of the literature discusses the diagnosis 
and treatment of this rare entity.
